# The canonical store: six base namespaces plus registered opaque mounts,
# residency semantics, and path edges for discovering cold base source.
"@context": "urn:bedrock:context/v1"
"@id": "urn:bedrock:vertex/situation-structure"
"@type": "urn:bedrock:ontology/SituationStructure"
label: "The situation structure"
statement: >
  situation/ is the repo's canonical law, current knowledge, and episodic
  history: six base namespaces plus registered opaque mounts. Bedrock
  validates every base source and only the mount boundary. AGENTS.md is the
  resident projection — definition, architecture, current risks, Decisions,
  mount registrations/linkage, and active Plan routing faces. Other Plans,
  episodic records, mount graph content, references, and bodies stay cold
  until a task follows a disclosed path.
path:
  - "urn:bedrock:path/situation/definition"
  - "urn:bedrock:path/situation/architecture"
  - "urn:bedrock:path/situation/risk"
  - "urn:bedrock:path/situation/plan"
  - "urn:bedrock:path/situation/record"
  - "urn:bedrock:path/situation/references"
